# Review: Supertraining Chapter 6, batch 6b (sections 6.4 to 6.8.2)

Reviewer: Claude Opus, independent falsification pass, 2026-10-03.
Scope: the 16 files in `staging/_scope_supertraining_ch6b.txt`.
Source: `staging/books/supertraining-6th-expanded.pdf`, PDF idx 347-362 (printed 336-351), plus PDF 305 and 381.

Method: I extracted the text layer for PDF 305, 347-362 and 381. I rendered and opened at 200 dpi PDF 348, 349, 351, 353, 354, 357, 358, 359, 360, 361 and 362, and the middle of 381. I also cropped Fig 6.22 and both panels of Fig 6.23 at 400 dpi and read values with pixel measurements (Fig 6.23 A: 11.12 px per 1%; B: 11.13 px per 1%; 64.3 to 64.6 px per week). I checked all 19 cited `method-baseline.md` lines (27, 30, 32, 59, 64, 75, 101, 105, 106, 115, 116, 117, 123, 151, 153, 171, 183, 185, 204). Every quote and tag matches. All 62 wikilink targets resolve. Each file has exactly six em dashes, all in the section headers, and no wikilink is wrapped across lines. Renders are in `staging/_renders/r6b_*.png`.

**PDF 359:** The writer read this page from the text layer only. I opened the page image, and the text layer matches it word for word for every quote used. (The adaptation definition, "adaptation cannot be considered an equilibrium process ...", is italic in the original.) The fixer can change "text layer only" to "checked against the page image" in the four entries that cite PDF 359.

**PDF 381:** I checked the image. The text says "prolonged stages (4-12 weeks)" for unidirectional training and "up to 2 months" for concentrated loading.

