ration-after-a-concentrated-block-before-the-next]]); 1-3 weeks is the latency to gains (PDF 305); 18-22 weeks is the stage needed to exhaust the CAR (PDF 360)." Keep the "three 3-4 week blocks give about 9-12 weeks" reconciliation, labelled Inference, as a link between block length (a) and stage length (b). Add as Inference: "5.3.3 and 6.12.2 both define loading as concentrated by one month's volume (23-25% of the annual volume, PDF 305, 381), which makes the month the working unit; 'up to 2 months' reads as a ceiling." Add the link [[claim--time-limits-of-single-emphasis-loading-by-motor-quality]]. |
| heuristic--restorative-stage-length-scales-with-homeostatic-disturbance | GO | Checked: the full restorative-stage quote against the PDF 361 / p.350 image, the "after the volume of loading is decreased" quote (PDF 360), the 1-3 week latency after 4-8 week blocks (PDF 305), and the 7-10 day pause (PDF 360). The Bompa & Haff quote matches the vault `allow-restoration` entry word for word. Baseline line 151 (Inferred) matches. The GPP mechanism is correctly marked as not given. The Example is labelled Inference. `supported` is right. | None. Minor: "as quoted in the 5.3.3 entry above" should read "as quoted in [[heuristic--allow-restoration-after-a-concentrated-block-before-the-next]]", since "above" means nothing in a standalone note. |
| claim--bondarchuk-50-percent-more-volume-did-not-prolong-training-effect | FIX | (1) Process note in the entry body: "The Table 6.1 and 6.2.2 material it points to is in batch 6a's pages (PDF pp. 334-336), not checked here." The brief forbids review or process history. (I confirmed that 6.2.2 starts on PDF 334 and Table 6.1 is referenced on PDF 335.) (2) Why it works opens "Bondarchuk's study as reported does not test intensity at all; the comparison with intensity is the authors' reading". That is a correct observation, but it is the writer's, presented without a label. Checked and correct: the full quote, including the italic "the importance of paying careful attention to zones of loading intensity" (PDF 361 image), and baseline line 105 (Inferred, "Not claimed in the interview"). The tension with the PDF 360 "more extensive ... the longer the new functional level is maintained" claim is accurate and labelled. `untested` is acceptable: one group, reported second-hand, with Bondarchuk's own "strictly" caveat. | (1) Replace the batch sentence with: "The 6.2.2 intensity-zone material and Table 6.1 it points to are at PDF pp. 334-336 / printed pp. 323-325." (2) Prefix "Inference:" to the first sentence of Why it works. |
